    "created_at": "2019-06-28T13:47:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-06-28T13:47:21Z",
    "body": "> User agents must implement the processing model of the prefetch keyword described in Resource Hints. [RESOURCEHINTS]\r\n\r\nIt seems this would need to be removed, right?\r\n\r\nIs the idea with prefetch still that subresources are also fetched (i.e., it's \"prenavigate\")? Wouldn't we have to create some kind of fake browsing context in that case? There's also a number of XSLeaks implications with this feature. Some of that seems to be already under consideration from the discussion I read, but it might be good to spell it out more clearly in a note or some such.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/506740212/reactions",
